{"id": "wwdc2017-251", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/251", "wordCount": 2687, "segments": [{"start": 18.0, "text": "Welcome to Now Playing and Remote Commands on tvOS."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "I'm Justin Voss, an engineer on"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "tvOS and in this talk we'll"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "cover how you can provide great"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "metadata and playback"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "experiences for your viewers."}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "First, let's talk about"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "providing Now Playing"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Having accurate and complete"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "metadata about your content will"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "help viewers to understand what"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "they're watching across a"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "variety of interfaces across"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "tvOS and iOS."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "The metadata you provide is"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "displayed in several places."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "For video content, the built-in"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "AVPlayerViewController displays"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "metadata along the top of the"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "video screen."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "For both video and audio content"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "the TV Remote app for iOS would"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "both display metadata and"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "playback controls."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "And for audio content, your"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "metadata will be displayed in a"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "badge in the corner of the"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "screen and as a full-screen"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "display when the user is idle."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Let's look at some screenshots"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "of these to better understand"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "them. In this screenshot, you can"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "already tell that we're watching"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "a WWDC talk from last year"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "because the metadata onscreen"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "makes that super clear."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "This is an example of using the"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "built-in AVPlayerViewController"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "for video content."}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "Here you can see the same talk,"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "but displayed in the TV Remote"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "app for iOS."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "You can also see the playback"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "controls which we'll cover later"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "in the talk."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "For audio content, when the Now"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "Playing information changes the"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "listener will see a notification"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "on their screen with the updated"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "metadata."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "In this screenshot here, you can"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "see what this would look like if"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "we were listening to an audio"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "only version of that WWDC talk."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "Finally, if the user puts down"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "the remote for a while tvOS will"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "automatically display the Now"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "Playing metadata in a"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "full-screen view like you see"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "here which really shows off the"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "artwork."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "So, hopefully I've convinced you"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "that providing the complete set"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "of Now Playing information is"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "worth your time."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "Let's talk about some of the"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "different ways you can do that."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "You have a few choices so it"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "depends on what kind of"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "technology you're using in your"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "Those of you using TVML can add"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "metadata using the MediaItem"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "JavaScript object."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "This object has several"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "properties on it for Now Playing"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "info, including a title,"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "subtitle and description, you"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "can provide a URL to an artwork"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "image and you can even provide"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "information about the content"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "rating such as PG-13 or R and"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "whether the content is explicit."}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "In the code sample, here you can"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "see that I'm creating a"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "MediaItem object with a URL to a"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "video and then configuring a"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "title and description on it and"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "providing a URL to an artwork"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "If you're using AVKit to play"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "your content you'll want to use"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "the AV metadata item class to"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "provide Now Playing info."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "For each piece of metadata you"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "want to provide, such as a title"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "or artwork, etcetera you'll"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "create an AV mutable metadata"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "item and configure several"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "properties on it."}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "You provide an identifier which"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "tells AVKit what kind of"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "metadata this represents."}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "This is how we know to tell the"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "difference between the object"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "that represents a title versus"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "the description and so on."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "You provide the value of the"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "metadata itself, which may be a"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "string or raw data bytes."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "You should set the"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "extendedLanguageTag to specify"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "what language the metadata is"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "intended for."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "Unless you have a good reason to"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "do otherwise we strongly"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "recommend that you use the value"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "und which means undefined."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "The way this property works is"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "that it will only be visible to"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "the user if the user's locale"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "matches the metadata's locale."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "So, for example, if you had a"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "movie that was produced in the"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "USA you may be tempted to"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "provide the title of that movie"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "with the language tag of English"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "since the title is in English."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "But if you did that then a"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "viewer in Germany wouldn't see"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "any title at all because the"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "metadata language doesn't match"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "their language."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "But if you had used the tag und"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "then everyone will see the"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "metadata regardless of their"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "language settings."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "Finally, in some cases you need"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "to give us a hint about how to"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "interpret the value you've"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "provided."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "In the case of providing artwork"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "image you'll give us the raw"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "bytes of the image as the value"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "and then use the dataType to"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "tell us if the image is a JPEG"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "or a PNG."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "Let's look at some code samples"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "to get a feel for how this"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "works."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Here you can see the code where"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "I'm creating an AV playerItem"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "and giving it a title and"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "description."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "In the first large code block"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "I'm creating an"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "AVMutableMetadataItem to"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "represent the title."}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "The first thing that I do is I"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "set the identifier to"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "AVMetadataCommon"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "IdentifierTitle so that AVKit"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "knows that this metadata item is"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "the title. Then I set the actual value as a"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "string."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "The AV metadata item API"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "requires these values to be NS"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "object types so casting the"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "string to an NSString."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "Finally, I'm setting the extendedLanguageTag to und"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "because the title of this talk"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "should appear the same"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "worldwide."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "In the second large code block,"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "I'm doing most of the same things to assign the"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "description."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "Other than providing a different"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "value you can see that on this"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "line I'm setting the identifier"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "to AVMetadataCommon"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "IdentifierDescription so that"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "AVKit knows how to interpret"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "this item."}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "Finally, on the last line I"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "assign an array of these"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "metadata items to the AV"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "playerItem's external metadata"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "If you wanted to provide the"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "release date of your content as"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "a metadata item you can do that"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "if you format your release date"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "as a string in a specific"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "format."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "This code sample shows you how"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "you can do that."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "Here you see that I'm creating"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "the date object for an arbitrary"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "date. Then I create a date formatter"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "and provide a specific date"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "format string here on this line."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "To create the metadata item, I"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "use the identifier"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "AVMetadataCommon"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "IdentifierCreationDate and"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "finally, I use the date"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "formatter to convert the date"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "object into a formatted string"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "and cast that string as an"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "NSString."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "Now in AVPlayerViewController"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "viewers will be able to see the"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "release year of the video"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "alongside the other Now Playing"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "info."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "Finally, here's an example of"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "how to provide image metadata"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "for your content."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "Here you can see that the first"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "thing I need to do is to get my"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "image as a data object."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "I'm doing that by loading the"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "image from a JPEG that's in my"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "app bundle, but you could get"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "your artwork from any source."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "Then to create the metadata item"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "the first thing I need to"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "specify is my identifier, which"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "in this case should be"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "AVMetadataCommon"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "IdentifierArtwork."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Next, I provide the artwork data"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "itself and cast the Swift data"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "object to an NSData."}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "Finally, to indicate what kind"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "of image this is I need to set"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "the dataType property."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "Since I know this image is a"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "JPEG I'm going to provide this"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "constant value here to indicate"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "that. Okay to give you a visual"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "reference of where some of these"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "items appear onscreen here's a"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "screenshot of the"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "AVPlayerViewController with some"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "annotations on it."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "The color coding will show where"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "each metadata identifier is"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "displayed."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "So, this is where the artwork"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "will be displayed, the title,"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "the creation date, and the"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "description."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "And here's a similar screenshot"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "of the TV Remote app."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "You can see here the Remote app"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "doesn't display exactly the same"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "set of metadata as"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "AVPlayerViewController."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "It displays the same artwork and"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "title, but instead of displaying"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "the description it instead"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "displays the artist and the"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "album name."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "You can see the AV foundation"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "identifiers to use here."}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "Okay that's all for AVKit."}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "If you're just playing your"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "video using some other"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "technology like Video Toolbox or"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "if you're playing audio only"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "content then you'll need another"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "way to provide Now Playing info."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "In those cases, you can use the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "MPNowPlayingInfoCenter."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "This is a singleton object that"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "has a dictionary property that"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "you can write your metadata"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "into."}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "So, there's a key for title, for"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "album name, for artwork and so"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "on. In addition to the metadata that"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "you are probably expecting you"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "can also specify explicitly if"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "the content is audio or video."}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "You can also provide some"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "information about the content"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "duration and the user's current"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "playback position."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "Your artwork is not provided as"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "raw bytes, but as an"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "MPMediaItemArtwork object which"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "we'll talk about more in just a"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "minute."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Finally, it's your"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "responsibility to update this"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "metadata dictionary as the"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "playback state changes."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "You do not need to update it"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "every second or even every"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "minute, but you should update it"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "when certain events occur."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "We recommend that you update it"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "when the currently playing item"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "changes, if any metadata about"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "the currently playing item"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "changes, such as the title or"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "artist name, if the user seeks"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "to a new position of the content"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "or if the playback rate changes"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "and finally, if playback begins"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "or stops."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some code."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "Here in the first code block,"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "I'm creating the object that's"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "going to represent my artwork."}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "The way this MPMediaItemArtwork"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "class works is that you provide"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "us with the native size of the"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "image in a block that we'll call"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "later with specific image sizes."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "The way this MPMediaItemArtwork"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "class works is that you provide"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "us with a native size of the"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "image in a block that we'll call"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "later with specific image sizes."}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "This block should return a"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "UIImage object that closely fits"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "inside the size that's passed to"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "the block."}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "So, for example, your app may"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "have downloaded several"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "different sizes of the same"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "artwork say in small, medium and"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "large sizes."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "When we call this block, you"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "should take the size we provide"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "and return the image that most"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "closely fits the requested size."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "We would discourage you from"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "trying to perform expensive"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "image resizing operations here,"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "just return the image that you"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "already have."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "In the second block of code,"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "this is where I'm actually"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "providing all of my metadata to"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "MPNowPlayingInfoCenter."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "You can see that this is just a"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "plain Swift dictionary with some"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "keys that are provided by the"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "framework and I'm simply"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "providing my values as regular"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "Swift types."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "There are two properties that I"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "want to call out in particular"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "though."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "The ElapsedPlaybackTime and the"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "PlaybackDuration."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Like I mentioned earlier, you"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "should provide these keys so"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "that tvOS knows how long your"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "content is and where the user is"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "currently at within the content."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "As various playback events occur"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "you should update the"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "ElapsedPlaybackTime to match"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "where the user currently is."}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "There's no AVPlayerViewController for this"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "API on tvOS, but I can show you"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "what this metadata looks like in"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "the TV Remote app."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "You can see where each property"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "is displayed onscreen."}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "These should look pretty familiar compared to the AVKit"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "version."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "Take note that in this version"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "though the scrubber bar is under"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "your control."}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "The ElapsedPlaybackTime and the"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "duration need to be provided by"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "your app to be displayed"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "correctly here."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "All right, let's change gears a bit now and talk about how your"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "app can handle external playback"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "commands."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Of course, your app will have"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "its own controls that the user"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "can interact with when your app"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "is displayed, but the user may"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "also want to control your app"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "from the TV Remote app on iOS or"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "if they're listening to"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "background audio from your app"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "on tvOS pressing the play pause"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "button on the Siri remote can"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "pause your app even while it's"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "in the background."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "To support these kinds of"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "interactions you will need to"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "make sure your app can handle"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "these Remote Commands."}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "The way to do that is with an API called"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "MPRemoteCommandCenter."}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "The way to do that is with an"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "API called"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "MPRemoteCommandCenter."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "This is another singleton object"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "that has a property for each"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "different kind of command that"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "your app can choose to support."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "For each command that you want"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "support you can register either"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "a target-action pair or a"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "callback block which will be"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "invoked when the command is"}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "performed."}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "If you provide a target-action"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "or a block the command is"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "assumed to be supported."}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "If you want to provide a handler"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "for the command, but need to"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "temporarily indicate that it's"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "not available you can mark it as"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "disabled. The method or block that you"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "provide must return an enum"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "value to indicate if your app"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "was able to successfully perform"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "the command."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "The definition of success here"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "is pretty broad."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "For example, if the user is"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "playing the last song in a"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "playlist and requests to skip to"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "the next track your app may"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "choose to simply end playback."}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "That would still be considered"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "successfully handling the"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "command so you should return the"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "success value in that case."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "Some commands like play and"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "pause are pretty simple."}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "If the handler for the pause"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "command is invoked it's pretty"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "clear what your app needs to do."}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "But other commands are more"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "flexible and both accept"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "parameters from your app and can"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "provide more parameters back to"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "your handler."}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "For example, the"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "MPSkipIntervalCommand is used to"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "allow the user to skip forward"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "or backward by several seconds."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "Your app can express a"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "preference for how many seconds"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "the user should be allowed to"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "skip."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "The skip command object allows"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "you to configure that"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "preference."}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "When the user actually performs"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "the skip command your handler"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "will be invoked with an object"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "parameter."}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "That object is of the type"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "MPSkipIntervalCommandEvent and"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "it has an interval property that"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "tells your app how many seconds"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "you should skip."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "And be careful this may not be"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "the same as the skip preference"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "you provided earlier."}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "Let's look at an example."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "Here's how an app might"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "implement the skip backward"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "command."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "You can see here that on the"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "first line I would prefer that"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "the user skips backward by 10"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "second intervals so I'm going to"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "assign the preferred intervals"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "property on the"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "SkipBackwardCommand object."}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "Then I'm going to provide my"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "handler block."}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "Now technically every command"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "handler receives the generic"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "type MPRemoteCommandEvent as the"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "parameter, but I need to cast it"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "to an MPSkipIntervalCommandEvent"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "so that I can get to its"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "interval property."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "Then I'm going to actually"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "perform the command."}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "In this sample, I'm playing my"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "content with an AVPlayer."}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "Since AVPlayer expresses its"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "time using CMTime structs that's"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "how I'm going to need to"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "calculate my new playback"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "position."}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "You can see here that I'm"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "getting the player's current composition then creating a new"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "CMTime struct with the skip"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "interval."}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "Finally, I'm subtracting that"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "interval from the current time."}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "I ask the player to seek to that"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "time and then return successful"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "from the command handler."}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "When the player finishes seeking"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "to the new time my completion"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "handler will be invoked and"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "that's where I'm going to update"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "my Now Playing info."}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "Remember, if we modify playback"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "state like seeking to a new time"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "we need to publish new Now"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "Playing info so we can update"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "the elapsed playback time."}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "Here I'm calling a function"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "called updateNowPlaying which"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "I'll show you on this next"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "slide."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "Here you can see how I'm going"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "to update my Now Playing info."}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "This is basically the same as"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "the example I showed you at the"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "beginning of this section, but"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "want to call out one specific"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "detail."}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "Here you can see that I'm using"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "the AVPlayer's current time"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "property in order to provide an"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "accurate value for the elapsed"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "playback time property."}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "In this case, since AVPlayer is"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "going to return a CMTime, but"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "MPNowPlayingInfoCenter requires"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "a floating-point value, that's"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "the number of elapsed seconds, I"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "need to use the CMTimeGetSeconds"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "function to convert the value."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "And that's all there is to"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "providing a great playback"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "experience with Remote Commands"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "and Now Playing information."}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "For more information, you can"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "visit the URL shown here to find"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "links to documentation and"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "related sessions."}]}